  <section|Status><label|status>

  Draft; passed independent bounded mathematical/source review at the exact
  conditional scope recorded below. This is not a pass on the upstream
  selected-history suppliers or the whole existence proof. Source revision is
  the imported <verbatim|source/upstream.json> pin
  <verbatim|3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464>. Owned manuscript:
  <verbatim|manuscript/existence/actual-marked-portfolio-calibration.tex>.

  <section|Source correspondence><label|source-correspondence>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>Public calibration caller: <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.figment>,
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Figment.lean>; it calls
    <verbatim|YM.Extra.Histories.Relay.antilles> on the same Music and
    terminal Cream.

    <item>Terminal pair and all-displacement identities:
    <verbatim|YM.Extra.Histories.Relay.pair/originate>,
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/Extra/SOURCE_HISTORIES/Counter.lean>.

    <item>Finite backward induction and signed difference:
    <verbatim|YM.Extra.Histories.Relay.eaves/antilles>,
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Antilles.lean>. The <verbatim|eaves>
    induction updates only the current scale; it preserves all higher states.
    <verbatim|antilles> then dualizes by the negative bottom primary and
    packages the Woke bounds.

    <item>Local response algebra: <verbatim|YM.Extra.Histories.Relay.acclaim>,
    <verbatim|Accord>, and <verbatim|Tones>,
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Accord.lean>. <verbatim|Answers.tunes> is
    the exact direction estimate and <verbatim|Answers.debt> is the exact
    pushed density identity. <verbatim|Tones.priced> is a Coupon for every
    keyed silent upper coefficient, with the exact budgets <verbatim|(eta*q,
    eta*q, 2*q)>.

    <item>Paid height and endpoint records:
    <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Freightage/Geyser> and
    <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Geyser.at>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Badlands.lean>.
    The selected public caller returns Music/Sung/Carol through
    <verbatim|Freightage.aim>; <verbatim|Geyser.heights> supplies the
    grade/period/volume height data, Brine, Cherry, Fiesta, Banks, support
    cover, and local-section insertion bound.

    <item>Actual local Coupon producer from a climbing door:
    <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Bandage.ravine>,
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Ravine.lean>. It uses
    <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Cub.clocksHere> in
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Crowding.lean> to obtain the finite Heading
    and <verbatim|Stampede>. Its main, regular, and forced clauses are
    assembled from <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Cub.jewelCard>
    (<verbatim|Rosin.lean>), <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Graces.basalCard>
    (<verbatim|Basal.lean>), and <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Graces.heavyK>
    (<verbatim|Beacon.lean>); the Heading price uses the seal/cap and leading
    price calculation in <verbatim|clocksHere>. The three-card local algebra
    is also recorded in the canonical heading-history handoff; it does not
    follow from the separate all-arity <verbatim|PayW> mixed compiler. Its
    exact premises include the Spring, Pitch, Pads, Decked, adjacent-jet,
    arrival, Cruise, main-test, Chop, tariff-budget, and compliance data
    passed by the climbing record. Then <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.asideP> in
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Gelatin.lean> to obtain
    <verbatim|Tones.priced>. The tuning inequality is the explicit rate bound
    in <verbatim|ravine>; the door soundness is <verbatim|sound_duet> from
    the climbing representation.

    <item>The Coupon-to-<verbatim|acclaim> passage is a finite algebraic
    construction: <verbatim|Accord.acclaim> sets the lower primary using the
    Coupon coefficient, cancels its density against the played correction,
    applies the Music cone bound and tuning inequality to charges, and unions
    the two finite Tale supports. This local argument is not itself the
    outstanding quantitative producer.

    <item>Terminal Cream to finite <verbatim|Yeast> conversion is
    <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.toast>, <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Croissant.lean>;
    its output fields are <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Yeast> in
    <verbatim|Bakery.lean>. The proof obtains keyedness from
    <verbatim|Challenge.chairs> and <verbatim|Sung.earned>, rate from the
    paid gain-chart/height inequalities, votes from the same-history
    <verbatim|Accord> coupon and <verbatim|Challenge.ships>, terminal
    attainment by adjoining the response booster and applying
    <verbatim|erected> plus the Banks allowance, and the terminal density
    identity from <verbatim|Relay.originate> and the selected Music readout.
    It requires the terminal Cream, the same <verbatim|Sung> Music and
    <verbatim|Challenge>, all adjacent <verbatim|Accord> witnesses,
    <verbatim|Banks>, endpoint support, and explicit paid height bounds;
    naming <verbatim|Yeast> alone does not prove those inputs.

    <item>Finite census/root conversion is
    <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Accent.baking> in
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Caprese.lean>, followed by
    <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Accent.filling> in <verbatim|Strudel.lean>.
    <verbatim|baking> gives the paid moment estimate for a finite mode under
    <verbatim|Migrating>, <verbatim|Occupancy>, <verbatim|Drake>,
    <verbatim|Fiesta>, <verbatim|Brine>, <verbatim|Moonlit>, monotone
    occupancy, and continuity. <verbatim|Stock.tallies> converts its
    extensive term to the number of census slots times the fourth-power side
    ratio. <verbatim|Stock.spacer> then takes the positive slot-count root
    and divides by the common marker weight. The five-unit per-slot constant
    uses the sharper <verbatim|Accent.toasted> response bounds (exponential
    price 2, forced price 1) and action reserve 1, so
    <math|2+1+2\<cdot\>1=5>; the generic price 3 would give 6. The manuscript
    states these finite hypotheses and root passage explicitly; they remain
    conditional on the same selected service record.

    <item>The exact producer assembled for the consumed <verbatim|Scrim>
    package is <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Inns.chaletrail>,
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Inns.lean>. Its hypotheses include Steam and
    Minty delay bounds, a monotone positive scale sequence, support-exponent
    floor 100, one nested selected history, all climbing-door witnesses, all
    same-history Freight records, and the fixed family making the action. It
    returns <verbatim|Scrim> and a separate price package.
    <verbatim|Bandage.nectar> (<verbatim|Stove.lean>) constructs
    <verbatim|Scrim.costs>: room/bank, initial Brine, monotone occupancy, and
    the all-level height package (Fiesta, Cherry, Banks, footprint cover and
    local-section placement bounds), plus terminal Music/forced-hook data
    from Freight. <verbatim|Bandage.ravine> (<verbatim|Ravine.lean>)
    constructs <verbatim|Scrim.listens> from a climbing door and its explicit
    rate inequality; it calls <verbatim|Cub.clocksHere>
    (<verbatim|Crowding.lean>) for the local Heading/Stampede input. The
    canonical three-card handoff is <verbatim|sec:three-port-history>, with
    equations <verbatim|eq:history-three-identities>,
    <verbatim|eq:history-common-waybill>, and
    <verbatim|eq:history-forced-price>; it is conditional on retained funded
    interpolation, slot realization and payments.

    <item>The all-degree/all-volume same-history Freight producer is
    <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Bandage.squad>,
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Marco.lean>. Given one Nest, delay cutoff,
    simple gauge group and all climbing doors, it constructs a Music from the
    chosen top voice using composition and the finite placement/cone
    estimate. Its Freight fields are top factory realization, Sung response
    history, Carol records and terminal forced hook. The final public
    consumer is <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.figment> in <verbatim|Figment.lean>,
    which consumes precisely <verbatim|Scrim> and the terminal Cream and then
    calls <verbatim|antilles>, <verbatim|toast>, and <verbatim|filling> on
    that same Music.

    <item>Room/bank interpolation arithmetic is
    <verbatim|YM.Work.G09.cone_cost> and <verbatim|cost_finest>,
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/Work/G09.lean>; the exact hypotheses are
    <verbatim|YM.Bid.roomCost> and <verbatim|YM.Bid.Bank>,
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/Bid/Loan.lean>.

    <item>The selected-run root test and marked-copy estimate are in
    <verbatim|manuscript/existence/centered-public-service.tex> and
    <verbatim|manuscript/existence/centered-construction.tex>, especially
    <verbatim|thm:ex-selected-run-service> and <verbatim|ex-centered-sail>.
  </itemize-minus>

  <section|Proof content and scope><label|proof-content-and-scope>

  The manuscript expands the terminal recentering, the cancellation in the
  terminal density and coordinate, the finite downward induction, and the
  room/bank cone arithmetic. It identifies the exact local response fields
  needed at every step and derives the marched-weight recurrence used in the
  root-test conversion. The public application fixes one family, one selected
  history, one period, one terminal volume, and one Music throughout; no
  volume-dependent reselection occurs in this argument.

  The chapter is conditional on the actual selected-run inputs. The canonical
  heading-history handoff proves local three-card algebra when its
  same-history Heading/Stampede and card premises are present; it is not the
  all-arity <verbatim|PayW> compiler. <verbatim|Inns.chaletrail> is the exact
  assembly for the <verbatim|Scrim> consumed by the final caller. Its
  immediate producers <verbatim|Marco.squad>, <verbatim|Bandage.nectar>, and
  <verbatim|Bandage.ravine> expose the precise upstream fields and
  hypotheses. The remaining obligation is to derive their common Nest,
  climbing doors, Freight, delay/payment data, and fixed-family making
  property from the selected funded history, uniformly in degree, period and
  volume, while retaining the same history through terminal Cream attachment.
  The three-card proof and the separate mixed compiler do not establish that
  selected-history attachment. The terminal and history attachment must be
  the original strong selected history, with no substitution by a restarted
  run. The one-step algebra, <verbatim|eaves>, terminal <verbatim|toast>,
  finite <verbatim|baking> lemma, and <verbatim|G09> cone inequality do not
  by themselves close these suppliers or the whole existence proof.

